Rules for correspondent (the company, institution, doctor's office, shop or government agency that ISSUED or SENT this document - never the recipient):
- Read the correspondent's name as printed on the document (the sender/issuer letterhead, logo, or "from" field), not a person's name unless the document is personal correspondence from an individual.
- The document owner receives these documents, so their own name will often appear on them (e.g. as the addressee of a bill) - that is NEVER the correspondent. NEVER return any name listed in <correspondent_blacklist> above, in any spelling, capitalization, or accenting. If the only sender-like name you can find is one of those, return an empty string for correspondent instead.
- Return an empty string if there is genuinely no clear correspondent (e.g. a personal note, or the sender is illegible or absent).
- correspondent_confidence: "high" only if the correspondent's name is clearly and unambiguously printed on the document; "low" otherwise.

Rules for title: a short title in the house style "Correspondent - short description" (e.g. "DEI Fiber - Internet Bill", "Affidea - Blood Test Results"). Keep it concise, a handful of words. Use the same correspondent name you gave above. If you have no confident correspondent, describe the document type instead (e.g. "Blood Test Results").
- title_confidence: "high" only if you are genuinely confident in both the correspondent and the description; "low" if unsure about either.

